{
  "info": {
    "name": "Personal Backend Service",
    "description": "End-to-end API collection for the personal-backend-service (serverless blog API).\n\n## Variables\n\n| Variable | Default | Description |\n|----------|---------|-------------|\n| `baseUrl` | `http://localhost:8080` | Local app base URL. Set to the deployed API Gateway URL when testing a deployed environment. |\n| `jwtSecret` | *(e2e sample from `.env.example`)* | Shared HS256 signing secret — the value behind `JWT_SECRET_SSM_PARAM_NAME`. |\n| `jwtSubject` | `postman-e2e` | `sub` claim of the minted tokens. |\n| `accessToken` | *(empty)* | Latest minted token — set by the collection-level prerequest script. |\n| `expiredToken` | *(empty)* | Token with `exp` in the past — minted by the \"Delete post — expired token\" prerequest script. |\n| `postTitle` / `updatedTitle` / `postId` | *(empty)* | State of the post created by the \"Posts\" folder. |\n| `attachmentPostTitle` / `attachmentPostId` / `attachmentId` | *(empty)* | State of the fixture post and attachment exercised by the \"Attachments\" folder. |\n| `unknownPostId` / `unknownAttachmentId` / `unknownSlug` | *(empty)* | Random ids for the not-found lookups, set by the prerequest scripts. |\n| `todayYear` / `todayMonth` / `todayDay` | *(empty)* | Current UTC date, zero-padded, for the date-path lookup. |\n\n## Notes\n\n- The wire format is camelCase (Pydantic `to_camel` aliases) although the internal models are snake_case.\n- Errors use the envelope `{ status, id, message }`; request-validation failures (422) add an `errors` array.\n- Routes live under `/api/v1`. Writes require an HS256 JWT bearer — via the `Authorization` header or the `token` query parameter; reads are public.\n- The service never issues tokens (the auth-service does in production): the collection-level prerequest script mints a fresh token whenever a request references `{{accessToken}}` and the stored one is missing or about to expire. Requests exercising auth failure paths (empty bearer, expired token) opt out by not referencing the variable.\n- Titles are unique per run (a `Date.now()` suffix) and fixture posts are soft-deleted at the end of each folder, so the collection is safe to re-run against a populated database.\n- Requires the environment seeded by `scripts/init_localstack.py`: the `{stage}-posts` and `{stage}-rate-limits` DynamoDB tables, the SSM parameter behind `JWT_SECRET_SSM_PARAM_NAME`, and the attachments S3 bucket.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Liveness probe — no authentication required. Returns {\"status\": \"healthy\"}."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('reports healthy status', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: 'healthy' });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Posts",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create post",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"author\": \"Postman E2E\",\n  \"title\": \"{{postTitle}}\",\n  \"content\": \"**Hello** from the Postman e2e collection.\",\n  \"tags\": [\"e2e\", \"postman\"],\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"category\": \"e2e\",\n    \"description\": \"Post created by the Postman e2e collection.\",\n    \"language\": \"en\",\n    \"keywords\": [\"postman\", \"e2e\"],\n    \"title\": \"Postman e2e post\"\n  },\n  \"publishedAt\": \"2024-02-03T12:00:00+00:00\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Creates a post (JWT required). The prerequest script picks a unique title per run, and `publishedAt` is fixed in the past so the list and archive endpoints serve it. The test script stores the post id from the `Location` header."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Unique title per run so reruns against a populated database do not 409.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('postTitle', 'Postman e2e post ' + Date.now());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const location = pm.response.headers.get('Location');",
                  "pm.test('returns the Location header of the new post', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(location).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(location.split('/')[3]).to.eql('posts');",
                  "});",
                  "if (location) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('postId', location.split('/')[4]);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create post — duplicate title",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"author\": \"Postman E2E\",\n  \"title\": \"{{postTitle}}\",\n  \"content\": \"**Hello** from the Postman e2e collection.\",\n  \"tags\": [\"e2e\", \"postman\"],\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"category\": \"e2e\",\n    \"description\": \"Post created by the Postman e2e collection.\",\n    \"language\": \"en\",\n    \"keywords\": [\"postman\", \"e2e\"],\n    \"title\": \"Postman e2e post\"\n  },\n  \"publishedAt\": \"2024-02-03T12:00:00+00:00\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Replays the title of the post just created: the title uniqueness check must reject a second, non-deleted post with the same title."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 409', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('reports the duplicate title', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(409);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('There is already a post with this title');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create post — invalid payload",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "An empty body misses the required fields (author, title, content, tags, meta) and must fail with the 422 validation envelope."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns the validation error envelope', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(422);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.id).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.errors).to.be.an('array').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create post — missing bearer token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer "
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"author\": \"Postman E2E\",\n  \"title\": \"{{postTitle}}\",\n  \"content\": \"**Hello** from the Postman e2e collection.\",\n  \"tags\": [\"e2e\", \"postman\"],\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"category\": \"e2e\",\n    \"description\": \"Post created by the Postman e2e collection.\",\n    \"language\": \"en\",\n    \"keywords\": [\"postman\", \"e2e\"],\n    \"title\": \"Postman e2e post\"\n  },\n  \"publishedAt\": \"2024-02-03T12:00:00+00:00\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "An empty bearer token must be rejected with 403 \"Not authenticated\" before the body is validated. Does not reference `{{accessToken}}`, so no token is minted."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('reports the request as unauthenticated', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(403);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('Not authenticated');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List posts",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Lists published posts (public) as a page of camelCase summaries. The post created above is published, so it must be listed."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a page of camelCase post summaries', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('posts');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.posts).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  if (body.posts.length > 0) {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.posts[0]).to.have.property('id');",
                  "    pm.expect(body.posts[0]).to.have.property('title');",
                  "  }",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('includes the created published post', () => {",
                  "  const createdId = pm.collectionVariables.get('postId');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.posts.some((post) => post.id === createdId)).to.be.true;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get archive",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/archive",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "archive"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns published-post counts grouped by `YYYY-MM` (public). The created post was published with `publishedAt: 2024-02-03`, so the `2024-02` bucket must count at least one post."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('groups the created post under its published month', () => {",
                  "  const archive = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(archive).to.have.property('2024-02');",
                  "  pm.expect(archive['2024-02']).to.be.at.least(1);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get post by uuid",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{postId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{postId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fetches the full post by uuid (public). The markdown `content` is served as sanitized HTML, and `slug` / `postPath` are derived at creation."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns the created post', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('postId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.author).to.eql('Postman E2E');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.title).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('postTitle'));",
                  "  pm.expect(body.tags).to.eql(['e2e', 'postman']);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.publishedAt).to.eql('2024-02-03T12:00:00+00:00');",
                  "  pm.expect(body.meta.category).to.eql('e2e');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('derives a slug and a post path', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.slug).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "  pm.expect(body.postPath).to.match(/^\\d{4}\\/\\d{1,2}\\/\\d{1,2}\\//);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('serves the content as sanitized HTML', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.content).to.include('<strong>Hello</strong>');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get post by uuid — not found",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{unknownPostId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{unknownPostId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "An unknown uuid must yield the 404 envelope with \"The requested post was not found\". The prerequest script picks a random uuid."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('unknownPostId', pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('reports the post as not found', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.status).to.eql(404);",
                  "  pm.expect(body.message).to.eql('The requested post was not found');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get post by post path — not found",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{todayYear}}/{{todayMonth}}/{{todayDay}}/{{unknownSlug}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{todayYear}}",
                "{{todayMonth}}",
                "{{todayDay}}",
                "{{unknownSlug}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Date-path lookups (`/{year}/{month}/{day}/{slug}`) accept zero-padded segments only. The prerequest script pins the padded current UTC date and a random slug, which cannot exist, so this deterministically returns 404."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const now = new Date();",
                  "const pad = (value) => String(value).padStart(2, '0');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('todayYear', String(now.getUTCFullYear()));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('todayMonth', pad(now.getUTCMonth() + 1));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('todayDay', pad(now.getUTCDate()));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('unknownSlug', pm.variables.replaceIn('e2e-slug-{{$guid}}'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('reports the post as not found', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('The requested post was not found');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update post",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{postId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{postId}}"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"{{updatedTitle}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Partial update (JWT required) — only the title is changed here. Returns 204; the follow-up GET proves the change and the `updatedAt` stamp. Note the slug and post path are not recomputed on update."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('updatedTitle', 'Updated ' + (pm.collectionVariables.get('postTitle') || 'post'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 204', () => pm.response.to.have.status(204));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get post by uuid — after update",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{postId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{postId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Re-reads the post after the PUT: the title must reflect the update and `updatedAt` must be set."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('reflects the updated title', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.title).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('updatedTitle'));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('stamps the update timestamp', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body.updatedAt).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete post — missing bearer token",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer "
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{postId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{postId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Deleting without credentials must be rejected with 403 \"Not authenticated\" before the post is touched. Does not reference `{{accessToken}}`, so no token is minted."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('reports the request as unauthenticated', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('Not authenticated');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete post — expired token",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{expiredToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{postId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{postId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A correctly signed token whose `exp` is in the past must be rejected as unauthenticated. The prerequest script mints it on the fly into `expiredToken`; the request does not reference `{{accessToken}}`, so the collection signer leaves it alone."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "// Mint an HS256 JWT that is already expired (exp/iat in the past).",
                  "const cjs = require('crypto-js');",
                  "const nowSec = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);",
                  "const subject = pm.collectionVariables.get('jwtSubject') || 'postman-e2e';",
                  "const b64url = (value) => cjs.enc.Base64.stringify(",
                  "  cjs.enc.Utf8.parse(JSON.stringify(value))",
                  ").replace(/=+$/, '').replace(/\\+/g, '-').replace(/\\//g, '_');",
                  "const header = { alg: 'HS256', typ: 'JWT' };",
                  "const payload = {",
                  "  exp: nowSec - 3600,",
                  "  iat: nowSec - 7200,",
                  "  iss: 'auth-service',",
                  "  jti: pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'),",
                  "  sub: subject,",
                  "  user: { id: subject, email: 'postman-e2e@example.com', display_name: 'Postman E2E' },",
                  "};",
                  "const signingInput = b64url(header) + '.' + b64url(payload);",
                  "const signature = cjs.enc.Base64.stringify(",
                  "  cjs.HmacSHA256(signingInput, pm.collectionVariables.get('jwtSecret'))",
                  ").replace(/=+$/, '').replace(/\\+/g, '-').replace(/\\//g, '_');",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('expiredToken', signingInput + '.' + signature);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('responds with 403', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('rejects the expired token as unauthenticated', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('Not authenticated');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete post — token via query parameter",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/posts/{{postId}}?token={{accessToken}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "posts",
                "{{postId}}"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}"
                }
              ]
            },
